# FIRST code-coverage measurement of this workspace.
#
# Nothing had ever measured coverage here, so nothing defended it: a change could
# delete a test, or add a large untested module, and every gate would stay green.
# tools/coverage_gate.sh now pins this as a floor.
#
commit   = f372d2fc05b25581ceb4934bf171bf60451d0632
host     = i265 (Core Ultra 7 265K, 20 threads, 30 GiB, x86_64 Linux)
date     = 2026-09-09
tool     = cargo-llvm-cov 0.9.1, cargo 1.98.1
command  = cargo llvm-cov nextest --workspace --locked --no-fail-fast --summary-only \
             --ignore-filename-regex '(tests?/|examples/|benches/)'
wall     = 216 s (run-heavy --mem 20G --jobs 10; peak RSS 1.12 GiB)

regions  = 173483 total, 14168 missed -> 91.83%
lines    = 126235 total, 10935 missed -> 91.34%
functions=   6896 total,   573 missed -> 91.69%

per crate (lines):
  svtav1           1068   40 uncovered   96.25%
  svtav1-cref     10716  407 uncovered   96.20%
  svtav1-dsp      25012 1094 uncovered   95.63%
  svtav1-encoder  88649 9329 uncovered   89.48%
  svtav1-target     297   36 uncovered   87.88%
  svtav1-types      493   29 uncovered   94.12%

# WHAT THIS NUMBER EXCLUDES — more important than the number itself.
#
# This is the `cargo nextest` surface ONLY. The 32 CI gate scripts, which are
# where the differential-vs-C verification actually lives, are NOT included.
#
# That is why the inter/video path reads as uncovered:
#   crates/svtav1-encoder/src/inter_md_arm.rs        434 lines   0.00%
#   crates/svtav1-encoder/src/leaf_funnel/ifs.rs     199 lines   0.00%
#   crates/svtav1-encoder/src/port_global_me.rs      204 uncov  49.25%
#   crates/svtav1-encoder/src/port_md/inject.rs      551 uncov  69.54%
#   crates/svtav1-encoder/src/inter_me/hme.rs        229 uncov  79.39%
# SVTAV1_INTER_EXPERIMENTAL is set by TEN gate scripts and by ZERO tests, because
# the public pipeline refuses multi-frame. Those lines are verified against C in
# CI, just not here. Likewise port_rc_vbr_cbr_update.rs (66%) and port_pass2_gop.rs
# (88%) are the deliberately-unwired rate control tracked by issue #22.
#
# Do NOT close that gap by flipping the env var in a test: dbgenv.rs resolves it
# once per process into a OnceLock, its own docs say it is not a feature flag and
# not for callers, and the stream it produces is known to diverge from C past the
# frame header. The honest reading is that the STILL-image surface is ~92% covered
# by fast local tests and the video surface is covered by C-differential gates.

# WHERE IT RUNS, and why not on push. MEASURED on the runner: the instrumented
# test run takes 1371 s (23 min) versus 216 s uninstrumented here -- llvm-cov is
# roughly 6x. The gates shards are the ~12 min critical path, so putting this on
# every push would take CI from ~12 min to ~23 and make coverage the critical
# path. It therefore runs NIGHTLY, on pull requests, and on demand. A push to main
# that deletes a test is caught by the next nightly, not immediately -- the
# deliberate trade for keeping the push path fast.
#
# The job also fetches the gb82-sc corpus (2.9 MB) and builds aomdec, because this
# floor was measured on a host where both resolve. Without the corpus,
# intrabc_output_is_tier_invariant_on_real_screen_content fails LOUDLY by design
# and the run aborts in 0.005 s; without aomdec the issue18_repro cells fail.
# Setting ZENAV1_SKIP_CORPUS_TESTS/ZENAV1_SKIP_DECODER_TESTS instead would make the
# measured number incomparable to the floor it is checked against.

# ANTI-VACUITY of the gate that pins this (measured, not asserted):
#   full suite                          91.83%
#   with the encoder_parity target gone 78.68%   (-13.15 points)
# The gate's slack is 0.50, so losing a single test target trips it loudly.
